    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm Dr. Smith. It's nice to meet you. Could you please tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Well, hello Dr. Smith. I, uh... I came in today mostly 'cause my wife insisted. See, it's about the men down at the domino table, and sometimes that announcer on the radio. They've been giving these little messages that are meant just for me. Warning me to be careful, you know? \n\nI listen to that radio every single morning. It's an old wooden one, a Zenith, I think. Got it at a hardware store years and years ago when they still sold good appliances. You just don't see craftsmanship like that anymore, everything is all cheap plastic now. My neighbor, he bought a plastic one and the knob broke off in a week. Can't even tune it. \n\nBut anyway, my wife, she says it is all just talk and I'm making it up, but I know they are warning me to be careful. She doesn't listen, though. She was too busy fussing with the garden this morning when I tried to tell her. The tomatoes are coming in real early this year because of the heat. We usually don't get them till late July, but the ground's been so dry...",
