    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "When you hear these messages on the radio, are you hearing actual voices speaking to you, or is it just that you are interpreting the words of the announcer as being directed at you?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "Well, the fella on the radio, he's just talking his regular broadcast talk, you know? But I know what he means. It's his words, but the warning is meant for me. \n\nBut... I suppose sometimes I do hear actual voices, too. Not from the Zenith, no. Like, some afternoons when the house gets real quiet... my wife usually goes to lie down around two o'clock. She's got a bad hip, you know. Needs a replacement but they say she's too old for the surgery now. It's a crying shame, she used to love to go walking down by the creek to look for those little painted turtles. \n\nAnyway, when it's quiet like that, I'll hear my old friend. He calls my name right from the front porch. Or sometimes he's just out there humming a choir song. It's clear as a bell, like he is standing right there by the screen door. We used to sing in the choir together, years and years ago. He had a deep baritone, could really rattle the pews. The church got a new pastor recently, a young kid from up north. Doesn't even wear a tie on Sundays! Can you imagine that? Standing up at the pulpit in just a regular shirt. I told my wife it ain't respectful for the Lord's house, but she says times are changing and I'm just being stubborn.",
