    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Aside from these experiences, how has your mood been lately—have you been feeling persistently down and hopeless, or perhaps unusually energetic and euphoric for weeks at a time?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S033",
      "patient_response": "Well, you know, it's funny you ask about energy. Some weeks, I wake up and I just feel... bright. Like I'm important, you know? I'll be laughing loud, talking a mile a minute. I feel like I could build a whole new shed out back if I wanted to. Speaking of sheds, the hinges on mine are rusting out completely. I told the boy at the hardware store I needed solid brass, but they sold me this cheap galvanized nonsense. It rained for three days straight last April, just poured and poured, and the water got right into the joints. Ruined a perfectly good bag of potting soil I had sitting in there. \n\nBut anyway, when I get like that, feeling all bright and fast... if my wife tries to slow me down or asks me too many questions, I get real sharp with her. I just snap. It's like I don't have the patience for it. She'll be asking me about what we're having for supper, and I'll just bite her head off. We usually have supper around five-thirty, right after the evening news. The fella who anchors the news now, he's got this terrible comb-over. You'd think with all the money they pay those television people, he could afford a decent haircut. My old barber, Frank, he used to give a proper trim for two dollars. Course, Frank passed away back in '98. Heart attack right there in the shop. Such a shame.",
